Quantitative studies of the conductivity of electrolyte solutions help us understand the nature of chemicals in solution. The conductive properties of a solution depend on factors such as the nature of the solvent or solute and temperature. It depends ultimately on ionic mobility and the capacity of ions to carry electric charge.
Conductivity measurements can help us obtain numerous chemical properties such as solubility or PH. This section addresses conductivity with an emphasis on how this property is measured in a chemistry laboratory.